From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000233 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 13:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: repair handoff and snapshot build boundaries

The first enabled owner-profile compile exposed two malformed declarations in
the canonical series. The snapshot helper passes a calibration cluster to a
calibration-table matcher but declares it as the unrelated state-cluster type.
The handoff supplier helper also loses its error-return and closing export
sequence when the series is applied. Restore those source boundaries without
adding any hardware access, provider registration, or runtime action.

This is a build-repair patch for the dormant owner profile. It is
experiment-only and not submission-ready.
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-handoff.c        | 3 +++
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-state-snapshot.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-handoff.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-handoff.c
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-handoff.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-handoff.c
@@ -1580,7 +1580,10 @@
 
 put_supplier:
 	put_device(&supplier->dev);
+	return ERR_PTR(ret);
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(mt6797_dvfsp_handoff_get);
 static int
 mt6797_dvfsp_state_provenance_check(
 	const struct mt6797_dvfsp_state_provenance *provenance)
 {
diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-state-snapshot.c b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-state-snapshot.c
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-state-snapshot.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6797-dvfsp-state-snapshot.c
@@ -76,7 +76,7 @@ static int mt6797_dvfsp_snapshot_cluster_check(
 	const struct mt6797_dvfsp_state_snapshot_input *input,
 	unsigned int cluster)
 {
-	const struct mt6797_dvfsp_state_cluster *calibration;
+	const struct mt6797_dvfsp_calibration_cluster *calibration;
 	const struct mt6797_dvfsp_clock_state_cluster *clock;
 	const struct mt6797_dvfsp_calibration_table_entry *matched_entry;
 	int ret;
-- 
2.43.0
